  "title": "Where State Efficiency Breaks Down Across Agency Systems",
  "summary": "State governments operate at enterprise scale, with systems that support millions of interactions across agencies and public touchpoints. As those systems evolve, more of the work required to keep them aligned falls to staff. Data moves across applications, and gaps in integration are often bridged manually. Teams route information, answer repeat questions, and navigate disconnected environments to keep operations moving. Over time, that coordination effort becomes a significant source...",
